  skin: [16, 60, 10.4, 6, 2.6, 0.7],// A CHIMNEY'S SKIN IS SIZED BY ITS DISTANCE FROM THE LINE (its axis to the laid line on the plan): within so many metres it is at its finest, beyond so many at its coarsest (between the two it coarsens fast at first: by the root of the way); at its finest it has so many corners to the round for each metre of its radius, at its coarsest so many; and so many rings for each metre of its height, at its coarsest so many
