// THE HOURS. One is chosen at build and holds for the visit: nothing of it is switched afterwards. Each gives the sky,
// the light the land takes from the sky (amb), the hour's KEY LIGHT (key: its colour on the land; moon: its colour on
// the steam and the plume; moonAt: its elevation and bearing, degrees, the bearing clockwise from north) and the
// fire's (fire), the flames' share of their height and how pale the hour makes them (flame), the lake's own glow (it
// is the hour's too: least in the moonless hour, when the water is a dark teal that carries the fires' images), the
// scene's thin haze (fog colour, density: none of this world's own materials takes it; they take the bowl's air, the
// table AIR, in every hour alike) and how much steam stands off every hot thing.
